&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Brand Strategy Lead owns the quality, consistency and distinctiveness of GetYourGuide&#39;s brand, partnering closely with Analytics, Customer Insights, Product, and Supply to keep the brand coherent globally and relevant locally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note this role is a individual contributor and will not be leading a team but leading and owning the brand frameworks and positioning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the brand framework - narrative, positioning and USPs.&lt;/strong&gt; Define what GetYourGuide stands for, what associations it is and is not building, and how the organisation reads progress against them.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Know the market and the customer, globally and locally.&lt;/strong&gt; Track competitive dynamics, category shifts, and how the Modern Explorer is changing, and turn genuine local differences into shared knowledge instead of market-specific narratives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Turn strategy into something the org can act on.&lt;/strong&gt; Build the chain from barrier → narrative angle → proof points → recommended levers, and keep the messaging hierarchy and narrative repository current as the source of truth for what&#39;s in, out, and true.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make the brand a resource, not a gatekeeper.&lt;/strong&gt; Package strategy so Product, Supply, Analytics, Customer Insights, and other teams can act on it directly, and bring narrative and CVP input into their roadmaps early enough to shape decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contribute to, and where relevant own, brand programs that build proof points.&lt;/strong&gt; Identify and help shape the research, partnerships, or flagship initiatives that generate real evidence for the narrative, working with Activation and other teams to bring them to life.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define how the org knows the brand is working.&lt;/strong&gt; Own the brand health and equity measurement framework — the scorecard that shows whether the narrative is landing, not just whether it shipped.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll be successful if you have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Judgment and taste,&lt;/strong&gt; the confidence to make narrative calls without a rulebook, and the discipline not to over-document strategy instead of deciding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sharp analytical instincts,&lt;/strong&gt; comfortable working with data and research directly, and skilled at turning market and customer understanding into strategic implications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Creativity and cultural fluency,&lt;/strong&gt; a feel for what&#39;s shifting in culture and category, and the instinct to find a fresh, distinctive angle on the CVP instead of defaulting to convention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong communication and stakeholder skills,&lt;/strong&gt; the emotional intelligence to build trust across Product, Supply, Analytics, and Creative, and get them to act on a shared narrative.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Great communication skills,&lt;/strong&gt; able to turn ambiguous strategic input into a clear, actionable plan that people outside the strategy team can build against.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program management&lt;/strong&gt; experience across various functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Excellent written and spoken communication in English&lt;/strong&gt;; additional languages are a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;8 years+ Brand strategy experience&lt;/strong&gt;: meaningful experience in brand strategy, positioning, or narrative development, ideally across multiple brands and markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agency experience is a plus.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience working with data analytics and insight &lt;/strong&gt;to direct research and translate insights into brand decisions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior IC track record,&lt;/strong&gt; comfort operating as a senior individual contributor with no direct reports — influence here comes from the quality of the thinking, not from headcount.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we’ll measure impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quality and consistency of our Brand Narrative across the organisation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Brand health targets defined with leadership and tracked transparently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successful collaboration &amp;amp; influence of internal teams (creative, supply, product, care).&lt;/li&gt;
