&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Come join our Comparison team as our Senior Product Designer! The Comparison team is a new strategic area of the business focused on our category verticals of our activities, like adventure tours or shows and events. This team will explore deepening our understanding of specific categories, distinct UX formats they need, and how we can best merchandise key information to our travelers. This will include how travelers make key decisions through social proof, developing proprietary data models, and all of the options available for the activities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our UX Team is a multi-disciplinary team of Product Designers, Content Designers, and UX Researchers passionate about solving customer problems in an effective and delightful way. We combine empathy, craft, and creativity to create valuable, usable, and delightful product experiences — guided by strong principles that make our work feel simple, trustworthy, human, and unique. We collaborate closely with Product, Engineering, and Data to ensure those principles are front and center in everything we build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and iterate on high-quality customer experiences across web and app, from discovery through to delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use qualitative and quantitative insights to make informed, outcome-focused design decisions — including running experiments and A/B tests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with UX Researchers to plan research initiatives and validate your designs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Content Design, your PM, and cross-functional partners to build shared understanding and drive alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and advocate for a strong, user-centred point of view on your product area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the design system — extending and refining shared patterns and components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to shaping the UX vision and 12-month direction for your product area, connecting your work to broader group strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor other designers and give constructive feedback that raises the quality bar across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
